6. Bank App\par
Project Overview\par
This is a React Native Banking Application that demonstrates the implementation of Redux for state management in a mobile environment. The app allows users to perform deposit and withdrawal operations, view their current balance, and track transaction history - all managed through a centralized Redux store.\par
\par
\f3\u-10180?\u-8233?\u-497?\f2  \f0 Architecture & Technology Stack\par
Technologies Used:\par
React Native - Cross-platform mobile framework\par
Redux - State management library\par
React-Redux - Official React bindings for Redux\par
React Navigation - Screen navigation\par
React Native Vector Icons - Icon library\par
React Native Linear Gradient - Gradient backgrounds\par
Data Flow Diagram\par
      User Action (Tap Button)\par
\f2     \f1\u8595?\f0\par
Event Handler (handleDeposit/handleWithdraw)\par
\f2     \f1\u8595?\f0\par
Validation (Check amount > 0, sufficient balance)\par
\f2     \f1\u8595?\f0\par
Dispatch Action (\{ type, payload \})\par
\f2     \f1\u8595?\f0\par
Reducer Processes Action\par
\f2     \f1\u8595?\f0\par
State Update (New balance + transaction)\par
\f2     \f1\u8595?\f0\par
UI Re-renders (useSelector triggers update)\par
\f2     \f1\u8595?\f0\par
User Sees Updated Balance & Transaction List\par
Design Elements:\par
Gradient Background: Linear gradient from blue to cyan\par
Card-based Layout: White cards with shadow for depth\par
Colour Coding:\par
Green for deposits (success)\par
Red for withdrawals (danger)\par
Material Icons: Clear visual indicators\par
User Experience:\par
Input Validation: Prevents invalid operations\par
Haptic Feedback: Vibration on successful transactions\par
Error Handling: Clear alerts for insufficient funds\par
Transaction History: Shows all operations with timestamps\par
Responsive Layout: Scrollable transaction list\par
Accessibility:\par
Large touch targets (buttons)\par
Clear contrast between elements\par
Descriptive placeholder text\par
Visual feedback on actions\par
\par
Testing Scenarios\par
1. Deposit Operations:\par
Valid positive amount \par
Zero amount \par
Negative amount \par
Large amounts \par
2. Withdraw Operations:\par
Amount \f1\u8804?\f2  \f0 balance \par
Amount > balance \par
Zero amount \par
Large amounts (within balance) \par
3. Transaction History:\par
Shows all transactions \par
Correct order \par
Correct icons and colours \par
Timestamps are accurate \par
4. Performance Optimizations\par
Memoization: Components re-render only when relevant state changes\par
Efficient List Rendering: FlatList/ScrollView for transaction history\par
Lazy Loading: Components load on demand\par
State Selectors: Only subscribe to needed state slices.\par
Conclusion\par
\par
The internship at Internforte Pvt. Ltd. was a transformative and enriching experience that allowed me to apply my academic learning in a real-world software development environment. Over the course of eight weeks, I contributed to the development of a Todo Application and Bank System using Redux Integration, where I gained hands-on experience with essential web technologies including HTML, CSS, JavaScript, React Native and Node.js.\par
This internship helped me understand how theory translates into practice, especially in areas like frontend design, backend logic, API development, and error handling.I also became more conscious of writing clean, modular code and designing user interfaces that are both functional and user-friendly.\par
Additionally, I developed important soft skills such as task management, time coordination, communication, and problem-solving. Weekly feedback from mentors improved my adaptability and ability to take constructive criticism positively. The agile development cycle we followed taught me the value of iterative progress and continuous improvement.\par
This internship has significantly boosted my confidence and technical readiness to take on future challenges\f2\emdash whether in internships, freelance opportunities, or full-time roles. I am sincerely thankful to my mentors, Mr. Rushabh Shah and Prof. Megha Dhotay, as well as the faculty at MIT-WPU, for their continuous support, feedback, and guidance throughout this journey.\par
